    {
      "startFrame": 0,
      "endFrame": 30,
      "text": "Did you know"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 30,
      "endFrame": 66,
      "text": "you can sleep in two countries"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 66,
      "endFrame": 102,
      "text": "at the same time?"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 102,
      "endFrame": 138,
      "text": "Switzerland has five neighbors:"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 138,
      "endFrame": 174,
      "text": "France, Germany,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 174,
      "endFrame": 210,
      "text": "Austria, Liechtenstein"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 210,
      "endFrame": 252,
      "text": "and Italy."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 252,
      "endFrame": 315,
      "text": "But its borders hide some strange surprises."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 315,
      "endFrame": 390,
      "text": "Liechtenstein is one of the world's smallest countries,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 390,
      "endFrame": 465,
      "text": "squeezed between Switzerland and Austria."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 465,
      "endFrame": 540,
      "text": "Its 40,000 people use the Swiss franc,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 540,
      "endFrame": 615,
      "text": "and Switzerland even runs its customs."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 615,
      "endFrame": 690,
      "text": "They're so close that in 2007,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 690,
      "endFrame": 765,
      "text": "about 170 Swiss soldiers got lost on a night march"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 765,
      "endFrame": 840,
      "text": "and accidentally invaded Liechtenstein."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 840,
      "endFrame": 915,
      "text": "Nobody minded — Liechtenstein doesn't even have an army."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 915,
      "endFrame": 990,
      "text": "Further north lies Lake Constance,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 990,
      "endFrame": 1065,
      "text": "shared by Switzerland, Germany and Austria."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1065,
      "endFrame": 1155,
      "text": "Yet the three never agreed where the borders on the lake are."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1155,
      "endFrame": 1260,
      "text": "It's one of the only places in Europe with no official border."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1260,
      "endFrame": 1335,
      "text": "Switzerland also swallows two foreign towns:"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1335,
      "endFrame": 1410,
      "text": "Büsingen, which belongs to Germany,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1410,
      "endFrame": 1485,
      "text": "and Campione d'Italia, which belongs to Italy."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1485,
      "endFrame": 1575,
      "text": "Both sit inside Switzerland — but neither is Swiss."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1575,
      "endFrame": 1650,
      "text": "But the strangest border runs through a hotel."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1650,
      "endFrame": 1740,
      "text": "In the village of La Cure stands the Hôtel Arbez."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1740,
      "endFrame": 1830,
      "text": "When a treaty moved the border in 1862,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1830,
      "endFrame": 1920,
      "text": "a building went up right on the new line."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 1920,
      "endFrame": 2025,
      "text": "Today the French–Swiss border runs straight through it."
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2025,
      "endFrame": 2130,
      "text": "In one room, the bed sits right on the border,"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2130,
      "endFrame": 2235,
      "text": "so guests sleep with their head in France"
    },
    {
      "startFrame": 2235,
      "endFrame": 2340,
      "text": "and their feet in Switzerland."
    }
  ],
